# 4.cut-fixture-cost

cut the repeated identical fixture work, with no change to what any test proves.

.why-this-order = parallelism multiplies whatever per-file cost remains. cut the cost
  first and the multiplier lands on a smaller number.

.guard = the per-file cost falls in the bench report, and compare reports zero lost
  cases.

.hardwon = intercept at ONE seam, not at 322 call sites. the fixtures call
  `npx rhachet roles link` 322 times for byte-identical output; rhachet routes that
  subcommand to run.jit, NOT to the compiled bun binary that roles boot|cost gets.
  a change at 322 call sites is 322 chances to alter what a test proves. the harness
  exports one shared execAsync — that is the seam.

.hardwon = keep the ORIGINAL path reachable behind an env switch
  (ACCEPTANCE_LINK_CACHE=off). a before/after measured on a tree that no longer exists
  is a claim nobody can re-check.
